# rpg/art/doll/clips/postures.clip: the 31 postures and Row on the adult bodies (POSES-B, P2b wave 2; STYLE_P2 13, 15, 16;
# VISION_PLAN 15.36 "The variety solution": a posture = a leg mode + arm keys + a prop + offsets). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# Frame counts and paces are postureInfo's (art_life.cpp); every facing natively (STYLE_P2 9); the elders take these with
# their own anchors (the stoop). The prop in hand is the doll's postureProp (doll_internal.h: the prop maps are PROPS');
# `held=<key>` names the gripping arm's key, so a prop map draws one view per key it is held in, anchored on the arm's
# `grip` mark (the left hand's `gripL`). The props (`role held <value>`) and the keys they are held in, every facing:
#   mug (mouth hold raise wave2) spoon bread (mouth hold) hammer woodaxe hoe (high low; woodaxe raise low) broom (low hold)
#   ladle (hold reach low pull) sack (shoulder) basket crate (hold) rod (reach hold) bowl (reach hold) lamppole (raise)
#   book (hold reach) linen (low hold) lute oud (hold low) fiddle (reach hold) harp (hold reach) flute pipes reed horn
#   (mouth) handbells (raise hold) framedrum bodhran (wave2 hold) taiko (high low) handdrums (hold low) gong (high reach)
#   clappers (hold pray) jingle (raise wave2). Carry's frames sway (sway=-1/0/1/0): a load declaring `sway <rows>` swings.
#
# Leg modes (maps/legs/adult/pose/std.pxm and tips.pxm, and the slice's `sit` in legs/adult/loco):
#   stand  legs=idle (the standing legs), or the walk / run keys for the striding postures (Carry, Play, Dance)
#   chair  legs=sit, bob=2: the hips on the seat line 7 rows over the floor (seatFit2's kSeat + 2), the feet on the floor
#          (SLICE-SIT-HEIGHT; the slice's Sit folded in here from clips/sit.clip)
#   floor  legs=cross, bob=8: cross-legged, the hips 2 rows over the floor or the cushion (seatFit2's floor seats)
#   kneel  legs=kneel, bob=5: on the left knee, the right foot planted (the head about 27 px)
#   ride   legs=ride, bob=2: astride, the thighs over the barrel, the boots in the stirrups (the hip mark on the saddle)
# Hang keys (the GARB areas' hangs): rest, sit, floor, kneel, ride. Sheath keys: rest standing and kneeling (facing down
# also seated), sit seated, floor and riding.
# Arm keys (maps/arms/adult/pose; the loco idle, lap, F, N, B, back and fwd): hold mouth raise wave wave2 pray reach pull
# high low shoulder knee (arms/adult/pose/man_r.pxm's header says what each is). Facing right the right arm is the near
# one (armL=- where the far arm hides behind the body); facing left the right hand still does the work, as the far arm,
# showing past the body (STYLE_P2 9: no thing changes hands between facings).

body man
# ---- Sit: the hands on the thighs (front and back), the near hand on the knee (sides); one frame
clip idle D posture sit
f armL=lap armR=lap hang=sit legs=sit neck=rest sheath=rest torso=rest bob=2
clip idle U posture sit
f armL=lap armR=lap hang=sit legs=sit neck=rest sheath=sit torso=rest bob=2
clip idle R posture sit
f armL=- armR=F hang=sit legs=sit neck=rest sheath=sit torso=rest bob=2
clip idle L posture sit
f armL=F armR=- hang=sit legs=sit neck=rest sheath=sit torso=rest bob=2

